{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-8-1","kind":"proposition","title":"连续比例数列与互素首末项","englishTitle":"If there be as many numbers as we please in continued proportion, and the extremes of them be prime to one another, the numbers are the least of those which have the same ratio with them.","book":8,"number":1,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.1","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.1/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":1,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","contentId":"euclid-8-1","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ce51520656663ebacf53935a13ed5d1316ad386b65c74a3f637bb71ff31afec7","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-8-1.statement","euclid-8-1.construction.1","euclid-8-1.proof.1","euclid-8-1.proof.2","euclid-8-1.proof.3","euclid-8-1.proof.4","euclid-8-1.proof.5","euclid-8-1.conclusion","euclid-8-1.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-8-1.statement","contentId":"euclid-8-1","revisionId":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"2d384750c03affde414add934140e60a6c51b49601aa7d0f6831a47fdbdac645","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If there be as many numbers as we please in continued proportion, and the extremes of them be prime to one another, the numbers are the least of those which have the same ratio with them."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果连比例个数字和互素个数字的极端数字是互素个,那么这些数字与它们的比是相同的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-1.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-8-1","revisionId":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"535c776cfbf0311c46723d79f3a4bdccb10f371450bd3b3032ddfc8fc96a4cd4","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let there be as many numbers as we please, A, B, C, D, in continued proportion, and let the extremes of them A, D be prime to one another; I say that A, B, C, D are the least of those which have the same ratio with them."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让我们想多少就有多少,A,B,C,D,连比例,让其中最极端的A,D,互素;我说,A,B,C,D是那些与它们具有同样比例的最小的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-1.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-8-1","revisionId":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7b0b73f4fa46cac08d15157a37d76f65e9971a14d47eb1c6851326d9b5104ebc","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if not, let E, F, G, H be less than A, B, C, D, and in the same ratio with them."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果不是,则E、F、G、H应少于A、B、C、D,并与其比例相同。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-1.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-8-1","revisionId":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b0fcf073baa8c8278987ac2bd4e75f92f432ef4472491819b4b900950a8d403d","citations":["euclid-7-14"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now, since A, B, C, D are in the same ratio with E, F, G, H, and the multitude of the numbers A, B, C, D is equal to the multitude of the numbers E, F, G, H, therefore, ex aequali, as A is to D, so is E to H. [[VII. 14](/principles/euclid-7-14)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,A,B,C,D与E,F,G,H处于相同比例,A,B,C,D与E,H的人数相同,因此,在平等的基础上,A对D的比例等于E对H；A 与 D 之比等于 E 与 H 之比。 [[VII. 14](/principles/euclid-7-14)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-1.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-8-1","revisionId":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0738b33ae97596d8db9d140d234fdbc3af5e0f0f924c2f50e412df79e7d0b7c0","citations":["euclid-7-21","euclid-7-20"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But A, D are prime, primes are also least, [[VII. 21](/principles/euclid-7-21)] and the least numbers measure those which have the same ratio the same number of times, the greater the greater and the less the less, that is, the antecedent the antecedent and the consequent the consequent. [[VII. 20](/principles/euclid-7-20)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但A,D是初级, 质数也是最低的, 而最小的整除个 , 相同比例的相同次数, 数量越大,数量越小,数量越小, 即, 早前的早, 以及随之而来的结果。 [[VII. 21](/principles/euclid-7-21)] [[VII. 20](/principles/euclid-7-20)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-1.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-8-1","revisionId":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"3c837b908ec13facd6b8956152d3f7c2444369f48fb869829b6609de4603b905","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore A measures E, the greater the less: which is impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,A 整除 E,数量越大,数量就越小:这是不可能的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-1.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-8-1","revisionId":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0ec9b7bf055df7c7d06befd96a233c6c6ea05dbae9c1a33d04052779264433ab","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore E, F, G, H which are less than A, B, C, D are not in the same ratio with them."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,E,F,G,H,即低于A,B,C,D与它们的比例不同。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-1.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-8-1","revisionId":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","order":7,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e38ef79d5e760b54f7a36bb90d52e5dac751e6e1c89b8a7d1519a5fdda5d2f8b","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore A, B, C, D are the least of those which have the same ratio with them. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,A,B,C,D与它们的比例最低。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-1.source","contentId":"euclid-8-1","revisionId":"euclid-8-1@raw-ce51520656663eba","order":8,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"eeb36d4b660e9a410959316cc130c4d9f00aeb3ed35b4bd2f2948618dfd00b48","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.1/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.1\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-8-1:euclid-7-14:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-1","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-1.proof.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-14","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.1","sourceUrl":"